          "html": "<p>Elon Musk, the CEO of SpaceX, Tesla, xAI, Neuralink, and X, has seen his estimated net worth fall below $900 billion, just weeks after making history as the world&#39;s first trillionaire.</p><p><br>Musk&#39;s fortune surged to unprecedented levels after SpaceX&#39;s initial public offering (IPO) sparked a rally that pushed the company&#39;s valuation above $2 trillion. </p><p></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrt4p98fc5ep07kysjijvh88\" alt=\"SpaceX-stock-price-decline-chart-showing-a-sharp-drop-in-share-value-as-investors-react-to-valuation-concerns-market-volatility-and-future-growth-expectations-580x1024.jpg\" title=\"SpaceX-stock-price-decline-chart-showing-a-sharp-drop-in-share-value-as-investors-react-to-valuation-concerns-market-volatility-and-future-growth-expectations-580x1024.jpg\" width=\"580\" height=\"1024\" /><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrt4o0rwc49107kyc289ovo7\" alt=\"1784545705314.jpg\" title=\"1784545705314.jpg\" width=\"682\" height=\"1024\" /><p>Because a significant portion of his wealth is tied to his ownership stakes in SpaceX and other technology companies, the rapid appreciation in the company&#39;s value briefly elevated his net worth beyond the $1 trillion mark.</p><p><br>However, recent weeks have seen a sharp correction in SpaceX&#39;s share price. Analysts attribute the decline to a combination of investor profit-taking after the stock&#39;s remarkable rally, concerns about the company&#39;s high capital expenditure, and broader volatility across global technology markets.</p><p></p><p> The sell-off significantly reduced the value of Musk&#39;s holdings, causing his estimated fortune to fall by more than $100 billion. Reports indicate that despite the decline, he remains the world&#39;s wealthiest individual.<br>Financial experts note that billionaire wealth is largely based on the market value of assets rather than cash. </p><p>As