      {
        "title": "Court Authorizes Police to Seize Cheddars Number One Oxford Street Hotel",
        "slug": "court-authorizes-police-to-seize-cheddars-number-one-oxford-street-hotel",
        "category": "General news",
        "publishedDate": "2026-07-22",
        "readTime": "2m read",
        "summary": "The legal battle over one of the most famous luxury properties in Accra has reached a critical point. The Accra High Court has officially granted the police permission to assist a Receiver in taking over the Number One Oxford Street Hotel. This drastic legal action stems from a massive 14.9 million dollar judgment debt that Kensington Residential Partners owes to Cola Holdings Limited. Even though the luxury property is tied up as mortgaged collateral, prominent businessman Nana Kwame Bediako, widely known as Cheddar, insists that the loan is strictly a corporate obligation and not a personal liability.",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p>The legal dispute over one of the most prominent luxury properties in the capital has reached a boiling point. The Accra High Court has officially authorized the police to step in and assist a designated Receiver in taking physical possession of the famous Number One Oxford Street Hotel.</p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrwlarig7x2v06mnpyrpv0ht\" alt=\"1784751445594.jpg\" title=\"1784751445594.jpg\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" /><p><br>​This major development follows a massive and drawn out financial disagreement. The court order is directly linked to a 14.9 million dollar judgment debt. According to the official court records, a company named Kensington Residential Partners owes this staggering amount to Cola Holdings Limited.</p><p></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrwlf04y846807me6wt7mbxi\" alt=\"1784755050848.jpg\" title=\"1784755050848.jpg\" width=\"1080\" height=\"986\" /><p><br>​Because the massive debt has remained unpaid, the creditors are now moving aggressively to secure their assets. The luxury hotel building itself was listed as the mortgaged collateral for the original loan agreement. Therefore, the Receiver now has the full backing of law enforcement to seize the property and begin the process of recovering the funds.</p><p><br><em><strong>​Corporate Obligation Versus Personal Liability</strong></em><br>​At the very center of this controversy is the prominent Ghanaian businessman Nana Kwame Bediako, who is popularly known across the country as Cheddar. Despite the heavy legal presence surrounding his flagship property, the entrepreneur is standing his ground regarding his own financial involvement.</p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrwlczw4830707me7woick2a\" alt=\"Screenshot_20260722_212009_Lite.png\" title=\"Screenshot_20260722_212009_Lite.png\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1081\" /><p><br>​Bediako maintains that the entire financial dispute is strictly business. He has publicly clarified that the multimillion dollar loan is purely a corporate obligation belonging to the company, rather than a personal debt tied to his individual finances.</p><p><br>​As the authorities prepare to execute the court order and secure the luxury hotel, the clear distinction between corporate responsibility and personal liability will likely remain a central talking point in this unfolding legal drama.</p>",
