      {
        "title": "Gomoa West Chiefs Back Captain Smart for NDC Parliamentary Ticket, Warn of Electoral Consequences",
        "slug": "gomoa-west-chiefs-back-captain-smart-for-ndc-parliamentary-ticket-warn-of-electoral-consequences",
        "category": "General news",
        "publishedDate": "2026-07-23",
        "readTime": "3m",
        "summary": "A section of traditional leaders in the Gomoa West Constituency has reportedly thrown its support behind media personality Captain Smart, urging delegates of the National Democratic Congress (NDC) to elect him as the party's parliamentary candidate. The chiefs believe his popularity and connection with constituents could strengthen the party's chances in the next general election.",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p>Some traditional leaders in the Gomoa West Constituency have publicly endorsed broadcaster Captain Smart for the National Democratic Congress (NDC) parliamentary ticket, urging party delegates to back his candidature ahead of the party&#39;s internal primaries.<br><br>According to the chiefs, Captain Smart possesses the visibility, grassroots appeal, and public influence needed to strengthen the NDC&#39;s chances of winning the parliamentary seat. They argue that the constituency requires a candidate capable of attracting both loyal party supporters and undecided voters, particularly in what is expected to be a fiercely contested election.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrxcyrxwmyr907mfctd07qu4\" alt=\"1784801821761.jpg\" title=\"1784801821761.jpg\" width=\"1080\" height=\"810\" /><p><br>The chiefs warned that overlooking Captain Smart during the selection process could prove costly for the party. In their view, failing to present what they describe as the strongest available candidate may hand the New Patriotic Party (NPP) an opportunity to retain or reclaim the seat.<br><a title=\"https://www.facebook.com/reel/27830788166554698/?app=fbl\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/reel/27830788166554698/?app=fbl\">Watch the video below as the chiefs pour Libation for Captain Smart</a></p><p><a title=\"https://www.facebook.com/reel/27830788166554698/?app=fbl\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/reel/27830788166554698/?app=fbl\">https://www.facebook.com/reel/27830788166554698/?app=fbl</a></p><p><br>Captain Smart, whose real name is Blessed Godsbrain Smart, is one of Ghana&#39;s most recognizable media personalities. Over the years, he has built a reputation for his outspoken commentary on governance, corruption, accountability, and social justice. His fearless approach to discussing national issues has earned him a large following, while also making him one of the country&#39;s most debated public figures.<br><br>His decision to venture into active politics has generated considerable interest across the political landscape. Supporters believe his popularity and direct engagement with ordinary Ghanaians could translate into electoral success, while others argue that winning elections requires more than media influence and public recognition.<br><br>The endorsement by the Gomoa West chiefs adds another dimension to the race for the NDC parliamentary ticket, highlighting the growing importance of community support ahead of the party&#39;s primaries. Although traditional leaders do not determine the outcome of the contest, their opinions often carry significant influence within their communities and can shape political conversations.<br><br>As the NDC prepares to choose its parliamentary candidate, attention will remain firmly on Gomoa West. The outcome of the primaries is expected to determine not only who leads the party into the next election but also how competitive the constituency will be when Ghanaians head to the polls.<br><br>Whether delegates heed the chiefs&#39; appeal or opt for another aspirant, the contest is shaping up to be one of the closely watched parliamentary races in the Central Region.<br></p>",
          "raw": {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
