                    "text": "\nCaptain Smart, whose real name is Blessed Godsbrain Smart, is one of Ghana's most recognizable media personalities. Over the years, he has built a reputation for his outspoken commentary on governance, corruption, accountability, and social justice. His fearless approach to discussing national issues has earned him a large following, while also making him one of the country's most debated public figures.\n\nHis decision to venture into active politics has generated considerable interest across the political landscape. Supporters believe his popularity and direct engagement with ordinary Ghanaians could translate into electoral success, while others argue that winning elections requires more than media influence and public recognition.\n\nThe endorsement by the Gomoa West chiefs adds another dimension to the race for the NDC parliamentary ticket, highlighting the growing importance of community support ahead of the party's primaries. Although traditional leaders do not determine the outcome of the contest, their opinions often carry significant influence within their communities and can shape political conversations.\n\nAs the NDC prepares to choose its parliamentary candidate, attention will remain firmly on Gomoa West. The outcome of the primaries is expected to determine not only who leads the party into the next election but also how competitive the constituency will be when Ghanaians head to the polls.\n\nWhether delegates heed the chiefs' appeal or opt for another aspirant, the contest is shaping up to be one of the closely watched parliamentary races in the Central Region.\n"
