ait until the investigation is concluded before making further decisions.\n\nIf the laboratory analysis confirms the initial roadside test, the player could face legal consequences under Australian law, in addition to potential disciplinary measures from football authorities. However, until those results are available, the matter remains under investigation.\n\nThe case has sparked widespread debate among football fans and the Australian sporting community, with many urging caution and emphasizing the importance of allowing the legal process to run its course before drawing conclusions.\n\nPublished by Orphe"
