        "content": {
          "html": "<p>The highly anticipated free agency saga surrounding LeBron James has finally reached a conclusion.</p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrzc2pe99njw07lgzrxzs25l\" alt=\"1784920559597.png\" title=\"1784920559597.png\" width=\"1376\" height=\"768\" /><p><br>The four time NBA champion has decided to join the Philadelphia 76ers for the upcoming season.<br>Rich Paul, the CEO of Klutch Sports Group and the agent for James, officially broke the news to Shams Charania of ESPN.</p><p><br>The financial terms of the agreement are quite surprising given the historical market value of the player.</p><p><br>James and the 76ers agreed to a two year deal worth a total value of 8 million dollars.<br>This minimum salary agreement also includes a player option for the second year.</p><p><br>In a statement released on social media, James referred to this move as his last decision.<br>He emphasized that his motivation is strictly about competing for a championship and not about financial gain.</p><p><br>He noted that he is not going for money or for family, but rather to have a chance at the feeling of winning another championship.<br>By adding James to their roster, the 76ers are making a massive push for their first NBA title since 1983.</p><p><br>He will be joining a highly talented starting lineup in Philadelphia.<br>According to sports analysts, the team will feature an incredibly strong core as James joins former MVP Joel Embiid alongside Tyrese Maxey, Jaylen Brown, and VJ Edgecombe.</p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmrzc3r119nok07lgceuzjhe1\" alt=\"458269705_921857053103335_7258512785192021374_n.jpg\" title=\"458269705_921857053103335_7258512785192021374_n.jpg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" /><p><br>Despite being forty one years old, James proved he still has plenty of ability left on the court during his previous season with the Los Angeles Lakers.<br>He played in sixty games an