n important affirmation of its mandate. The full judgment is expected to provide further legal clarity on the constitutional basis of the OSP's prosecutorial authority.\n\nThe ruling is widely regarded as a landmark decision in Ghana's ongoing efforts to combat corruption and strengthen the rule of law.\n\nSource: Supreme Court of Ghana / Office of the Special Prosecutor (OSP)\n\n"
