              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "One of the most cinematic and heavily contested allegations in the entire trial involved Obaatanpa Microfinance Limited. According to court records and testimonies, MASLOC issued an Agricultural Development Bank (ADB) cheque for GH¢500,000 as an investment in Obaatanpa on July 24, 2014. However, the state alleged that shortly after the cheque was received, Tamakloe-Attionu demanded a staggering 24% interest rate on the investment—a rate so high that Obaatanpa deemed it unprofitable and decided to return the principal."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "During the trial, a star witness for the prosecution, Seth Obugyei, testified that when Obaatanpa attempted to return the money via a formal cheque, Tamakloe-Attionu insisted on receiving the refund in cash. Obugyei told the court that he physically handed over GH¢500,000 in cash, stuffed into a checkered 'Ghana Must Go' bag, to the accused at a filling station on the Spintex Road in Accra. The prosecution argued this money was never deposited back into MASLOC's accounts, effectively meaning it was stolen by the CEO."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "To corroborate this, Francis Bandoh, the Head of the Finance Unit at MASLOC, testified that he routinely wrote to Obaatanpa on a quarterly basis requesting the payment of interest on the GH¢500,000 investment, completely unaware that the principal had allegedly been returned in cash. Bandoh testified that Obaatanpa never responded to these requests, and when he pressed Tamakloe-Attionu about it, she allegedly brushed it off, claiming it was a \"special project\" she was handling directly."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading-three",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "2. The Mac Autos Fleet and Massive Price Inflation"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
