        "readTime": "3m read",
        "summary": " Apam Senior High School has officially been upgraded to a Category A school. Great APASS grew from a tiny cocoa shed into one of Ghana's top educational powerhouses.",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p>The government has officially upgraded the school to Category A. This means the Ghana Education Service now recognizes it as one of the very best high schools in the entire country.<br></p><p>While the students and teachers are celebrating this huge win today, the school, proudly known as &quot;Great APASS,&quot; did not start at the top. Its story is actually very inspiring.</p><p>Apam SHS opened its doors on February 20, 1953. It was started by the late Rev. J.W. DeGraft-Johnson. Back then, there was no massive campus or modern buildings.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm0bxqvefxt07l35mnyez04\" alt=\"3333.webp\" title=\"3333.webp\" width=\"202\" height=\"250\" /><p>The very first 20 students took their classes inside a small cocoa shed at a place called Apaa Paado. It started as a simple day school with only two teachers.</p><p>By 1960, the school had grown and moved to its beautiful current home, a location known as &quot;Mbofra mfa Adwen&quot;.</p><p>The famous headmaster Peter Augustus Owiredu took over, and under his strong leadership, people started calling the school &quot;Great APASS&quot;. In 1964, the school added boarding houses, which allowed students from all over the country to travel there to learn.</p><p>The new Category A status is a well-deserved reward for the school&#39;s hard work. The students truly live by their motto, &quot;Obrapa gya owura kwan,&quot; which means &quot;Character and Efficiency&quot;.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm0fzohf30s06mj813ffo6t\" alt=\"iiii.jpg\" title=\"iiii.jpg\" width=\"554\" height=\"554\" /><p>The school has had several headteachers who transformed and helped structure Great APASS. This includes Esther Hamilton, who coined the famous APASS phrase known as &quot;Marketing,&quot; which simply means an interaction between a boy and a girl. Consequently, she was followed by leaders like Jemima Atta Elsie Morrison and the current headmistress, Comfort Essah Amoafoh, who is still guiding the school to greater heights.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm3wb0fg5k606mju77yb0os\" alt=\"vhvvhvh.jpg\" title=\"vhvvhvh.jpg\" width=\"548\" height=\"364\" /><p>Recently, their achievements have been nothing short of incredible. The Apam Robotics team made it to the national finals and earned a spot to represent Ghana at a huge World Championship in Michigan, United States.</p><p>Their brilliant Science and Maths (NSMQ) team even defeated the famous Mfantsipim Boys SHS to reach the national competition.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm0gxpgei5307l3ngtgaqz0\" alt=\"images1111.jpg\" title=\"images1111.jpg\" width=\"533\" height=\"375\" /><p>The students also get top grades, with some achieving truly historic results. In 2021, an exceptional student named NasiruDeen Ghartey graduated from Apam SHS with a perfect 8 As.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm0k1acedab06juv267uzj8\" alt=\"G8g3od3XkAAhv0t.jpg\" title=\"G8g3od3XkAAhv0t.jpg\" width=\"900\" height=\"732\" /><p>He then went on to the University of Cape Coast, where he recently graduated as the valedictorian with a flawless 4.0 CGPA. His performance was so outstanding that the Acting Vice-Chancellor, Professor Denis Worlanyo Aheto, publicly pledged to personally sponsor his further studies abroad.  </p><p>Because of its great training, this school has also produced some of Ghana&#39;s most important leaders. Top judges like former Chief Justice Kwasi Anin-Yeboah and Supreme Court Justice Nene Amegatcher went to school here.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm0muytf55d06mj8xryt5ir\" alt=\"images.webp\" title=\"images.webp\" width=\"704\" height=\"435\" /><p>It is also the former high school of famous politician Aaron Mike Oquaye, rich businessman Nana Kwame Bediako, and popular musician Guru.<br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsm0qph3el1207l3f8is9bce\" alt=\"46ec9b4a60bb66092aedc3b5fa4a03a2.jpg\" title=\"46ec9b4a60bb66092aedc3b5fa4a03a2.jpg\" width=\"600\" height=\"600\" /><p>From a tiny shed in 1953 to a powerful Category A school today, Great APASS keeps proving why it is one of the best places to learn in Ghana.<br></p><p><br>Obrapa ! Gya Owura Kwan!</p>",
