        "title": "IGP Promotes 25 Police Officers for Stopping Robbers and Seizing Cocaine",
        "slug": "igp-promotes-25-police-officers-for-stopping-robbers-and-seizing-cocaine",
        "category": "World",
        "publishedDate": "2026-08-10",
        "readTime": "2m Read",
        "summary": "The Inspector General of Police has promoted 25 officers to reward them for busting armed robbery groups and intercepting illegal cocaine.",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p>The Inspector General of Police (IGP), Christian Tetteh Yohuno, has officially promoted 25 police officers to new, higher ranks. This is a huge honor, and they earned it by doing some very dangerous and important work to keep the country safe.  </p><p></p><p>So, why did these specific officers get promoted? They were recognized for their bravery in two major areas.</p><p>First, a group of these officers played a huge part in tracking down and busting armed robbery syndicates. These are organized groups of dangerous criminals who attack and steal from innocent people in communities and on the highways.  </p><p></p><p>Second, other officers were rewarded for their incredible work in stopping illegal drugs from hitting the streets. They successfully intercepted hidden shipments of suspected cocaine. To give you an idea of how big these drug busts can be, in one recent operation, officers managed to seize wrapped slabs of suspected cocaine worth over 1 million Ghana Cedis.  </p><p></p><p>The IGP and the top police leaders personally congratulated the officers for their bravery and discipline.  </p><p></p><p>By giving out these promotions, the police leadership is sending a very clear message to the rest of the force: if you work hard, stay professional, and risk your life to protect the nation, your excellent work will be noticed and rewarded</p>",
          "raw": {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
