        "title": "Disaster Avoided: Firefighters Prevent Massive 45,000-Litre Fuel Explosion in Tamale",
        "slug": "disaster-avoided-firefighters-prevent-massive-45000-litre-fuel-explosion-in-tamale",
        "category": "World",
        "publishedDate": "2026-08-11",
        "readTime": "3m read",
        "summary": "Heroic firefighters in Tamale successfully rescued two people and prevented a massive explosion after a tanker carrying 45,000 litres of diesel overturned.",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p>A team of heroic firefighters just saved the day and prevented what could have been a massive disaster in Tamale.</p><p>On Tuesday, a huge fuel tanker completely overturned on the road at Adubili Yili.  <br></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsp3iz0s3ile07mo7swvbf2a\" alt=\"772792814_2111247269488565_5723558125522659999_n.jpg\" title=\"772792814_2111247269488565_5723558125522659999_n.jpg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\" /><p>This was an incredibly dangerous situation. The truck was carrying about 45,000 litres of highly flammable diesel, making it a ticking time bomb.  </p><p></p><p>The driver and his assistant were trapped inside the wrecked vehicle. Thankfully, crew members from the Ghana National Fire Service (GNFS) Northern Regional Headquarters rushed to the scene immediately.  </p><p></p><p>The firefighters quickly sprang into action. They successfully pulled the two trapped men out of the truck and handed them over to the National Ambulance Service so they could get urgent medical care.  </p><p></p><p>But the danger was not over yet. Diesel was spilling everywhere.</p><p>To stop a deadly fire or a massive explosion from wiping out the area, the fire crew carefully cooled down the tanker and worked hard to contain all the spilled fuel.  </p><p></p><p>Things actually got even more chaotic during the rescue operation. Out of nowhere, two passenger buses collided right next to the accident scene.  </p><p></p><p>One of those buses even slammed into a parked fire truck, damaging its air system.  </p><p></p><p>Amazingly, despite the extra crash and all the chaos, no additional people were hurt in that second accident.  </p><p></p><p>Following this wild rescue, the Fire Service issued a strong warning to all drivers. They are begging motorists to slow down and be extremely careful around accident scenes so emergency workers have enough safe space to do their jobs and save lives.</p>",
