        "content": {
          "html": "<p>Cristiano Ronaldo is a married man! The football legend has finally tied the knot with his longtime partner, Georgina Rodríguez.</p><p>The happy couple got married on August 11, 2026, in a quiet, private civil ceremony in Cascais, Portugal. Interestingly, the timing of the wedding is very special. They said their vows exactly one year to the day after announcing their engagement on August 11, 2025.  </p><p></p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsp69cma4jmy07mojgckxwfw\" alt=\"WhatsApp Image 2026-08-11 at 21.23.33.jpeg\" title=\"WhatsApp Image 2026-08-11 at 21.23.33.jpeg\" width=\"720\" height=\"900\" /><p>Shortly after the ceremony, they shared the exciting news with the world on Instagram. The couple posted a sweet picture showing off their new wedding rings with a simple caption that read: &quot;C❤️G&quot;. Keeping it a very intimate family event, all five of their children were there to celebrate the special moment with them.</p><p>Looking back, the newlyweds have a great love story. They first met in 2016 while Georgina was working at a Gucci store in Madrid, and they have been together ever since.</p><p>Leading up to their big day, there was actually a very funny mix-up regarding the wedding. Just a few days before the real ceremony, a wild rumor spread online claiming they were getting married on August 8 at a historic church in Ronaldo&#39;s hometown of Madeira. As a result, thousands of excited fans rushed to the church to see the famous couple. However, they ended up accidentally crashing the wedding of a regular local couple! The poor bride and groom had to push their way through a massive crowd just to get to their own ceremony.  <br></p><p>Now, after that funny mix-up and nearly a decade of dating, the global football icon and his beautiful bride are finally husband and wife</p>",
