      {
        "title": "Tragic News: Ghanaian Evacuee Passes Away Upon Arrival in Accra",
        "slug": "tragic-news-ghanaian-evacuee-passes-away-upon-arrival-in-accra",
        "category": "World",
        "publishedDate": "2026-08-15",
        "readTime": "2m Read",
        "summary": ": A Ghanaian who was evacuated from South Africa sadly passed away shortly after arriving at the Kotoka International Airport in Accra on Friday evening",
        "content": {
          "html": "<p>The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has shared some very heartbreaking news. A Ghanaian citizen who was being evacuated from South Africa has tragically died right after arriving in Accra.  </p><img src=\"https://eu-west-2.graphassets.com/cmrmsa7zm00ij01wc3pwrgjxy/cmsuau1yr5e6a06jqyy3hxjzr\" alt=\"774461363_1571790038321650_7560453441365365824_n.jpg\" title=\"774461363_1571790038321650_7560453441365365824_n.jpg\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1126\" /><p>This sad event happened on the evening of Friday, August 14, 2026. The passenger was part of a group of 50 Ghanaians flying back home on an Air Tanzania flight. They were returning to Ghana to escape the recent attacks on foreigners in South Africa.  </p><p></p><p>According to the official statement from the Ministry, other passengers noticed something was wrong during the trip. They reported that the person started feeling very sick about 30 minutes before the airplane even landed.  </p><p></p><p>The flight officially touched down at the Kotoka International Airport at 5:50 p.m. A medical emergency team was already on standby at the airport waiting to receive the passengers. They immediately rushed to help the sick person and tried everything they could to save his life.  </p><p></p><p>Sadly, their rescue attempts were not successful. Doctors confirmed that the passenger passed away at the airport&#39;s Emergency Medical Reception at exactly 6:55 p.m.  </p><p></p><p>The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated that they are currently handling the formal process of contacting the family of the deceased. In the meantime, the person&#39;s body has been safely moved to the Police Hospital so medical experts can perform an autopsy to find out exactly why he died.  </p><p></p><p>The Ghanaian government has been working very hard to bring over 1,600 citizens back home safely from South Africa, completely paying for the flights to protect them. While the rescue missions have been largely successful, this sudden loss is a very sad moment for the nation.</p>",
          "raw": {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has shared some very heartbreaking news. A Ghanaian citizen who was being evacuated from South Africa has tragically died right after arriving in Accra.  "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
